        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-24 09:21:04.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-7880 utils: show target load with lfs df --stats",
        "message": "LU-7880 utils: show target load with lfs df --stats\n\nAdd \"lfs df --stats\" to print the read and write bandwidth and\nRPCs/s that each MDT and OST returns in statfs, with \"-v\" also\nshowing the peak values.  The values can also be selected with\n\"lfs df --output=read_bw,write_bw,read_ops,write_ops\" and the\n*_max fields.  Targets that do not return the stats are shown\nwith \"-\", and the summary line is the sum over all targets.\n\nllapi_obd_fstatfs() requests the full struct obd_statfs only when\nthe caller passes LL_STATFS_PERFSTATS, and retries without it on\nolder client modules that only accept the original size.\n\nAlso check the number of fields given to \"lfs df --output\", which\ncould overflow the field_order[] array, and size it for all fields.\nSort the \"lfs df\" options by their short option.\n\nAdd sanity test_861 to check that the stats change with IO.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=861,HONOR_EXCEPT=y serverversion=2.17\nFixes: a3f05d81f603 (\"LU-18243 lfs: Add --output and --no-header options to lfs df command\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I48a918522c1d53c95af126123360179e5b3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
